{"reference":"Genesis 2","book":"Genesis","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Adam and Eve in later interpretation","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A later epistolary reading invokes Adam's formation and Eve's deception when giving a command, but the way that reading grounds a local or universal rule remains disputed. The Genesis account should therefore be read on its own terms before drawing a broader rule from this reception history.","verse_refs":["Genesis 2:7-25"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_002_01a7446ba49bac52683a8e61"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
